# Fusion Installer MPPM patch

- **Fusion version:** 2.1.3 (Build 2390, `Fusion.Runtime 2.1.3.0`)
- **File:** `Assets/Photon/Fusion/Editor/Fusion.Unity.Editor.cs`
- **Region:** `Assets/Photon/Fusion/Editor/FusionInstaller.cs`, `static FusionInstaller()`
- **Marker:** `ROOTBOUND_PATCH(FusionInstaller-MPPM)`

## Why

Fusion's `[InitializeOnLoad] FusionInstaller` static constructor reads
`<project>/Packages/manifest.json` **unconditionally** (line ~15541) to decide
whether to install `com.unity.nuget.mono-cecil` and set scripting defines.

MPPM virtual players (`Library/VP/mppm*/`) are launched with `-noUpm` and
`-library-redirect ../..`, and MPPM creates the `Packages` directory **empty**
(`VirtualProjectFileRepository.CreateProject`, line 54). There is no manifest, so
`File.ReadAllText` throws `FileNotFoundException` in the static constructor
during virtual-player activation:

```
System.IO.FileNotFoundException: Could not find file ".../Library/VP/mppm.../Packages/manifest.json"
  at System.IO.File.ReadAllText
  at Fusion.Editor.FusionInstaller..cctor () [Fusion.Unity.Editor.cs:15541]
```

The installer's package/define work is unnecessary in a virtual player: UPM is
disabled and packages/defines are inherited from the main project (symlinked
`ProjectSettings`, redirected `Library`).

## Patch (before -> after)

Before:

```csharp
static FusionInstaller() {
  if (PlayerSettings.runInBackground == false) {
    FusionEditorLog.LogInstaller($"Setting {nameof(PlayerSettings)}.{nameof(PlayerSettings.runInBackground)} to true");
    PlayerSettings.runInBackground = true;
  }

  var manifest = Path.Combine(Path.GetDirectoryName(Application.dataPath) ?? string.Empty, PackagesDir, ManifestFile);

  if (File.ReadAllText(manifest).Contains(PackageToSearch)) {
    UpdateDefinesForAllTargets();
  } else {
    FusionEditorLog.LogInstaller($"Installing '{PackageToInstall}' package");
    Client.Add(PackageToInstall);
  }
}
```

After:

```csharp
static FusionInstaller() {
  // ROOTBOUND_PATCH(FusionInstaller-MPPM)
  var manifest = Path.Combine(Path.GetDirectoryName(Application.dataPath) ?? string.Empty, PackagesDir, ManifestFile);

  if (!File.Exists(manifest) && FusionMppm.Status == FusionMppmStatus.VirtualInstance) {
    FusionEditorLog.LogInstaller($"Fusion: no {ManifestFile} (MPPM virtual project); skipping package installation.");
    return;
  }

  if (PlayerSettings.runInBackground == false) {
    FusionEditorLog.LogInstaller($"Setting {nameof(PlayerSettings)}.{nameof(PlayerSettings.runInBackground)} to true");
    PlayerSettings.runInBackground = true;
  }

  if (!File.Exists(manifest)) {
    Debug.LogError($"[Fusion] {ManifestFile} not found at '{manifest}' and this is not an MPPM virtual project. " +
                   $"Add '{PackageToInstall}' to the project manifest, then restart Unity.");
    return;
  }

  if (File.ReadAllText(manifest).Contains(PackageToSearch)) {
    UpdateDefinesForAllTargets();
  } else {
    FusionEditorLog.LogInstaller($"Installing '{PackageToInstall}' package");
    Client.Add(PackageToInstall);
  }
}
```

Notes:
- Uses Fusion's supported MPPM API `FusionMppm.Status` (no ad-hoc folder-name match
  of our own); MPPM itself is identified by the package's own logic.
- The virtual-player branch returns **before any write** (`runInBackground` included).
- Main Editor with a manifest: original behavior preserved.
- Other context without a manifest: actionable `Debug.LogError`, no silent swallow.
- No exceptions are caught/swallowed; no manifest is created or copied.

## Reapply after SDK updates

Fusion ships this as generated source inside the `.unitypackage`; a Fusion
reimport/update **overwrites** the file and removes the patch.

1. Keep `Assets/Photon` in version control (checkpointed with the project).
2. After any Fusion SDK update, reapply the "After" snippet above.
3. Verify presence (read-only): menu `Rootbound > Verify Fusion MPPM Patch`, the
   PlayMode test `FusionInstallerPatchPresenceTests`, or
   `grep "ROOTBOUND_PATCH(FusionInstaller-MPPM)" Assets/Photon/Fusion/Editor/Fusion.Unity.Editor.cs`.

No automatic vendor-code rewriting is performed.
